1qt4|v|To cook by exposure to radiant heat before a fire; as, to roast meat on a spit, or in an oven open toward the fire and having reflecting surfaces within; also, to cook in a close oven. ; To cook by surrounding with hot embers, ashes, sand, etc.; as, to roast a potato in ashes. ; To dry and parch by exposure to heat; as, to roast coffee; to roast chestnuts, or peanuts. ; Hence, to heat to excess; to heat violently; to burn. ; To dissipate by heat the volatile parts of, as ores. ; To banter severely. ; To cook meat, fish, etc., by heat, as before the fire or in an oven. ; To undergo the process of being roasted.	o:6u9,125,1~6u9,125,1
