1qua|n|One who rocks; specifically, one who rocks a cradle. ; One of the curving pieces of wood or metal on which a cradle, chair, etc., rocks. ; Any implement or machine working with a rocking motion, as a trough mounted on rockers for separating gold dust from gravel, etc., by agitation in water. ; A play horse on rockers; a rocking-horse. ; A chair mounted on rockers; a rocking-chair. ; A skate with a curved blade, somewhat resembling in shape the rocker of a cradle. ; Same as Rock shaft.	a:1uoi,74,3~1uoi,74,3	V:203j,30,2~203j,30,2	n:27q1,84,106;22ko,69,4;1iym,42,3;fdl,27,3~27q1,84,106;22ko,69,4;fdl,27,3;1iym,42,3	N:16ms,105,5;uoq,81,3;9uk,52,3;203j,48,7;69o,33,3;9ud,27,3;14cl,14,2~203j,48,7;16ms,105,5;9uk,52,3;uoq,81,3;69o,33,3;9ud,27,3;14cl,14,2
